{
  "requirement": "When `habeas author` assesses a subject with existing evidence, that evidence\nMUST only determine whether the subject needs assessment. Its inputs,\ndetermination, and rationale MUST NOT contribute to the mandatory input set\ndefined by {cite}`requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs` or otherwise be\nsupplied to the model. A new assessment's evidence MUST record only the inputs\nsupplied to it, so sources that an earlier assessment read but that no longer\nexist or are no longer relevant cannot block or shape reassessment.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no gap. The code and tests below cover each obligation in `requirements.ci.authoring_inputs`.\n\n**Obligation 1: existing evidence MUST only determine whether the subject needs assessment.**\n- `select_subjects` (`src/authoring/batch.rs`) and `subject_is_current` (same file) load the existing evidence through `LoadedDetailEvidence` and ask `current(...)`. They use the result only to decide whether to select the subject or count it as unchanged.\n- `run_batch`, reached through `author_all_with_options`, never passes the evidence content to the assessment.\n- `AssessmentSources::prepare` (`src/authoring/inputs.rs`) does not read the subject's evidence file at all.\n- The comment in `prepare` says so (\"Existing evidence only decides whether to reassess; its inputs are not carried forward\").\n\n**Obligation 2: the evidence's inputs, determination, and rationale MUST NOT contribute to the mandatory input set or be supplied to the model.**\n- `prepare` builds the mandatory set from the subject declaration, `{cite}` targets, `{impl}`/`{test}`/`{fixme}` edges, anchors, term definitions, and built-ins. None of these come from evidence content.\n- Generated evidence files are dropped from the set by `omit_generated_evidence`, `generated_evidence_path`, and `generated_evidence_selector`.\n- Tests:\n  - `bundle_combines_direct_references_terms_and_current_existing_selectors` writes old evidence with a determination, rationale, and a `notes.txt` input. It asserts that `notes.txt` and \"old secret judgment\" are absent from the mandatory inputs.\n  - `earlier_evidence_inputs_and_judgments_are_not_carried_forward` asserts that neither \"notes.txt\", \"evidence/\", nor the old rationale appears in the supplied inputs. It also asserts the old file is unchanged.\n\n**Obligation 3: the new assessment's evidence MUST record only the inputs supplied to it.**\n- `converse` (`src/authoring/mod.rs`) calls `sources.record_inputs(&pending)` only after a successful response. `pending` holds the mandatory inputs plus tool deliveries.\n- `record_inputs` fills `recorded`, and `record()` writes `sources.recorded_inputs()` into the evidence.\n- Nothing from earlier evidence enters `recorded`.\n- Tests: the first test above asserts `recorded_inputs()` is empty at preparation, and `definitions_introduced_by_a_read_are_supplied_and_recorded_before_submission` checks what gets recorded.\n\n**Obligation 4: sources that an earlier assessment read but that no longer exist or are no longer relevant cannot block or shape reassessment.**\n- `prepare` never resolves earlier evidence inputs, so missing files or items cannot cause an error.\n- Test: `unresolvable_earlier_inputs_do_not_block_reassessment` plants earlier inputs for a missing file, a removed item, and a removed requirement. `prepare` still succeeds, and the mandatory inputs are exactly the subject's own declaration.\n\n**Marking.** The code that carries these obligations out has `{impl}` references to the requirement: `prepare`, `omit_generated_evidence`, `generated_evidence_path`, `generated_evidence_selector`, `source_input`, `converse`, and `author_all_with_options`. The three tests have `{test}` references. I found no unmarked implementing code or unmarked tests. I also found no unspecified behavior.",
  "references": "50148c9cfa29314fa2a17847f5b31dd0d0dbff0707c70e2e20cb993a124bd5c8",
  "inputs": [
